{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `InspectionContext` method and exposes it to the agent\nas the `read_node` command.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> InspectionContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Read the contents of this graph node.\n    pub fn read(&self, node: &D::NodeId) -> Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two structural obligations. Both are met.\n\n1. **Method signature.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#impl[InspectionContext<'d, D>]/fn[read]` is a `pub fn read(&self, node: &D::NodeId) -> Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error>`.\n   - It sits in `impl<'d, D: Domain> InspectionContext<'d, D>`, which matches the required receiver, parameter and return types.\n   - `D::NodeId`, `D::NodeContent` and `D::Error` are associated types of `Domain` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]`.\n   - `read` returns the `content` of `read_snapshot`, so it yields `D::NodeContent`.\n\n2. **Exposure to the agent as `read_node`.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[tools]` defines a tool named `read_node`. It takes a `path` parameter.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` handles the `\"read_node\"` command. It resolves the node, calls `InspectionContext::prepare_read` and returns the node content to the agent.\n   - `prepare_read` is the same underlying read that `read_snapshot` uses, and `read` calls `read_snapshot`. `dispatch` calls `prepare_read` directly rather than `read`, so that it can defer recording until delivery. The text does not require delegation through `read`, so I do not count this as a gap.\n\nNo {fixme} acknowledgments apply. This is a structural assessment only. I did not assess behavior or test evidence, and the `read_node.behavior` and `read_node.inputs` requirements are separate declarations.",
